ryan: Quick sync on docs PR #859 — adding a migration section and cleaning up SDK snippets for function/tool calling + structured output. I pushed a draft but tests are red. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/859

emma: I looked — failing snippet tests and markdownlint. The TS snippet is throwing `ReferenceError: parseJson is not defined`. Also there's a leftover anchor to `/docs/outputs#schema` that 404s.

noah: I can fix the TS import and run the snippets locally. Which runtime change do we need to call out in the migration note?

ryan: Runtime change summary: tool invocations used to come back as top-level `function_call`; new responses include `response.actions` array, where tool calls are objects with `type: "tool_call"` and `payload` or `args`. We should show both old->new mappings and an SDK-compatible compatibility snippet.

emma: Draft mapping example I put in the PR:```ts
// compatibility helper
export function normalizeToolCall(resp: any) {
  // prefer new shape
  const actions = resp?.response?.actions || [];
  const tool = actions.find((a: any) => a.type === 'tool_call');
  if (tool) return { name: tool.tool_name || tool.name, args: tool.args || tool.payload };
  // fallback to old shape
  if (resp.function_call) return { name: resp.function_call.name, args: resp.function_call.arguments };
  return null;
}
```

ci-bot: snippet tests failed  docs/tests/snippets/test_ts_snippets.py: TypeError in example parsing. markdownlint: MD013/line-length on docs/structured-output.md: line 210.

noah: I'll shorten the long lines and add the missing import: `import { parseJson } from '@redwood/inference-sdk'`. Also change example to read `parseJson(resp, 'response.actions[0].args')` so it matches the runtime path.

ryan: Good. Also we need to explain guardrails vs strict schema: one-line suggestion: "Guardrails are runtime heuristics and enforcement helpers intended to guide model outputs (best-effort). JSON Schema validation is a strict contract that may cause the request to be rejected or the response to be considered invalid." Put that in the structured-output intro.

emma: Suggest a small "fail-soft" example so teams can warn instead of hard-fail. Draft:```json
{"guardrails":{"mode":"warn","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"summary":{"type":"string"}}}}}
```

noah: For the SDK snippet we should show a TypeScript example of parsing and handling missing fields gracefully:```ts
import { Client, parseJson } from '@redwood/inference-sdk'
const c = new Client()
const res = await c.generate({ model: 'gpt-x', prompt: 'Find docs' })
const toolArgs = parseJson(res, 'response.actions[0].args')
if (toolArgs) {
  // safe to call tool
} else {
  // fallback
}
```

ryan: Two more minor things: 1) update any internal links from `/docs/outputs` to `/docs/structured-output`, 2) add a short changelog blurb explaining that we'll support both shapes for two releases and point to normalizeToolCall helper.

